## 4. Proposed Change Plan

The following actions summarize the main changes required.

| Step | Action | Expected result |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Correct terminology throughout the document. | Consistent use of Risk Sources and SR/OV terminology. |
| 2 | Reorganize the document around the Initial SR/OV Inventory. | A clearer structure aligned with the reference prototype. |
| 3 | Review the 11 identified risk sources. | A validated list of internal and external sources. |
| 4 | Cross-reference all 31 Workshop 1 Feared Events with the risk sources. | A systematic SR/OV inventory. |
| 5 | Review the 17 currently unrepresented events. | An explicit coverage decision for every feared event. |
| 6 | Revise the SR/OV descriptions and severity references. | Clearer and more traceable relationships between SR, OV, and ER. |
| 7 | Reconsider the evaluation and scoring document. | Scoring based on the revised and validated inventory, if retained. |

---

## 5. Conclusion

The current Workshop 2 document provides a useful initial identification of risk sources and their target objectives. It also establishes relationships with several feared events identified in Workshop 1.

However, the current inventory references only 14 of the 31 Feared Events. This makes a systematic coverage review necessary before the SR/OV inventory can be considered complete.

The main priority should therefore be to reorganize and rebuild the inventory through cross-referencing the Workshop 1 Feared Events with the internal and external sources of risk identified in Workshop 2.

The evaluation and scoring stage should follow this work, rather than being finalized on the basis of the current incomplete inventory.

**The objective is to establish a coherent and traceable SR/OV inventory that provides a reliable foundation for the subsequent EBIOS-RM workshops.**
